# Declared projections (bd-lyih).
#
# The commit guard's bead-hunk attribution rule requires every bd-* token
# ADDED by the staged diff to appear in the commit message. That is right for
# work this repository performs. It is wrong for a file a GENERATOR wrote, so
# those are declared here and the guard stops charging this repo for bead ids
# that belong to whoever fed the generator.
#
# `linguist-generated=true` is the ecosystem's existing marker for exactly
# this, which is why it is reused rather than a toron-private format. The
# guard evaluates it per path, last match wins, and REFUSES any pattern that
# would also match compiled source — so this file cannot be used to switch the
# rule off for the crates.
#
# Only genuinely machine-written files belong here. A hand-written file that
# mentions a foreign bead id still owes attribution; see toron-core's
# `mailbox::guard` tests for the negative control that proves it.

# `toron catalog --json` output. Contains no bead ids (the
# catalog_no_internal_ids gate keeps it that way) but it is rewritten wholesale
# on every surface change, so the exemption is here to survive the next one.
docs/catalog/toron-mcp.json linguist-generated=true

